{"name":"Boeing Blue","hex":"#3d4652","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boeing","blocks":[{"text":"The Boeing Company is an American multinational corporation that designs and manufactures airplanes, rotorcraft, rockets, satellites, and missiles worldwide. The company also provides leasing and product support services. Boeing is among the largest global aerospace manufacturers; it is the fourth-largest defense contractor in the world based on 2022 revenue and is the largest exporter in the United States by dollar value. Boeing was founded in 1916 by William E. Boeing in Seattle, Washington. The present corporation is the result of the Boeing acquisition of McDonnell Douglas on August 1, 1997."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Boeing_Virginia_Headquarters_%28cropped_and_brighter%29.jpg/330px-Boeing_Virginia_Headquarters_%28cropped_and_brighter%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boeing","wikidata":"Q66"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Boeing_Plant_in_Renton%2C_5-18-2010_%284622746048%29.jpg/500px-Boeing_Plant_in_Renton%2C_5-18-2010_%284622746048%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Boeing_Plant_in_Renton%2C_5-18-2010_%284622746048%29.jpg/1280px-Boeing_Plant_in_Renton%2C_5-18-2010_%284622746048%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Boeing_Plant_in_Renton%2C_5-18-2010_%284622746048%29.jpg/500px-Boeing_Plant_in_Renton%2C_5-18-2010_%284622746048%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Assembly of a 737 in the Boeing Renton Factory","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoeing_Plant_in_Renton%2C_5-18-2010_(4622746048).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Final_assembly_of_Boeing_737_airplane_%281975%29.jpg/500px-Final_assembly_of_Boeing_737_airplane_%281975%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Final_assembly_of_Boeing_737_airplane_%281975%29.jpg/1280px-Final_assembly_of_Boeing_737_airplane_%281975%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Final_assembly_of_Boeing_737_airplane_%281975%29.jpg/500px-Final_as